CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*member operator requires.*<<type:auto>>.*$
--
Verifies that range-based-for `auto` deduction handles qualified
forms (`const auto&`, `auto&`, `auto*`).  Without the fix, only
bare `auto` was deduced; qualified forms stayed as
`merged_type(const, auto)` and any member access on the loop
variable failed with
  member operator requires struct/union type on left hand side
  but got '<<type:auto>>'
breaking iteration over class-typed containers using the canonical
`for(const auto& x : container)` idiom.
